            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0581" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.003/632: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ruddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-12T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 12,
                                1921—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received July 12—6:55
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>256. Your 157, June 28th [<hi rendition="#italic">26th</hi>], 6 p.m.,
                        1920.<anchor n="76" xml:id="d418-f1"/> Chinese Government now requests
                    Governments concerned to proceed in perfect accord with second revision of
                    customs schedule to effective 5 percent as provided by commission of 1918. No
                    reference made to likin abolition.</p>
                <p>Request authorization indicate assent if other powers agree.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ruddock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
